  "name": "Death Grips",
  "editorial_article": "Formed in Sacramento during the summer of 2010, Death Grips began their experimental hip-hop career with the December 2010 track \"Full Moon (Death Classic),\" which they noted coincided with a total lunar eclipse and the winter solstice. The trio—Stefan Burnett (MC Ride), Zach Hill, and Andy Morin—developed a reputation for chaotic, abrasive sound design and aggressive, high-energy performances. After signing with Epic Records in 2012, the band gained notoriety for leaking their second album, No Love Deep Web, via BitTorrent in defiance of the label's release schedule, ultimately leading to their departure from the company. Their discography is characterized by self-released mixtapes and albums often featuring unconventional sampling; for instance, Niggas on the Moon utilizes \"found object\" vocal samples from Björk, while the track \"Birds\" contains a guitar performance by Robert Pattinson recorded on an iPhone. Following a purported disbandment in 2014, the group returned to release records like 2016's Bottomless Pit and 2018's Year of the Snitch. In 2025, the band confirmed their continued activity, explicitly refuting rumors of a permanent break-up after an internal leak, and announced work on a new studio album in November of that year.",
